ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119771 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050283 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119772 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050283 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119784 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050283 #edb/ref 1031 "Triangular Matrices" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050283 #edb/ref 1033 1777 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050283 #edb/ref 1034 0.9149892976448922 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050283 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "3cb2a10b-5d06-5efe-b222-3c14b0ccd7c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050727 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048122 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050727 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050727 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049970 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050727 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050727 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050283 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050727 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050911 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050727 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050972 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050727 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059743 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050727 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059744 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050727 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059745 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050727 #edb/ref 1031 "The Transpose of a Matrix" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050727 #edb/ref 1033 232 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050727 #edb/ref 1034 1.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050727 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "6197c039-5830-56a2-b171-eac0f7516ad1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119585 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4394" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119585 #edb/ref 1071 "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n![](images/fc/fc2ed708d717844ca73b7ecbfd8467923fad091ae524153350e7e2fb3df1ea4e.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119585 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fe3edf12-af5b-5bb0-b5b3-efb6cd809134" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119585 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries above the diagonal are $0$'s:\n![](images/52/5260137f2dbf20b44400659be8467da333ff228e5bff323465f920a9505ee5f2.png)\n\nTherefore, it is a lower triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not an upper triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element below the diagonal: $a_{21}=6 \\neq 0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119586 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4395" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119586 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following matrices are lower triangular matrices?\n\n![](images/ad/ad9636de9b8c93338350a6b99d88476b481ed1bf03a5dd64935abedbdb626524.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119586 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d7c263d4-5d0a-52cd-b876-cfa3bd3171e0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119586 #edb/ref 1074 "The matrix $B$ is a lower triangular matrix since all the entries above the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nThe matrices $A$ and $C$ are *not* lower triangular matrices since they each have a non-zero element above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{23} & =1\\ne 0 \\\\ {c}_{13} & =1\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119598 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4498" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119598 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix \n![](images/4d/4dd9b1c1b3d789c166ecd8f6d2a909609c7f4324705c84115cce84a29181bf32.png)\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ is upper triangular\n\n- $A$ is lower triangular\n\n- $A^T-A$ is lower triangular" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119598 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "205d32a2-ac26-5eaf-896a-c6182a70eff7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119598 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false, since $A$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n![](images/c1/c1ec838cd30cca8fbb2e3996d5a7d84dadb233e1951d05b532a9d606d887eb2f.png)\n\n- Statement II is true, since all the entries above the main diagonal are zeros:\n![](images/f3/f39c68a9b1f5e16caffbf159b629a958e147e14099334b049bdfcd857eef84d2.png)\n\n- Statement III is false, since the result of $A^T-A$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n![](images/f4/f4415c87201f5b92f23e3320c313cd58ac4e720135928645896f976614c5eaa0.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119771 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048252 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119771 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120120 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119771 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120121 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119771 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262602 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119771 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119771 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186269144 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119771 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186269145 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119771 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186269148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119771 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186269149 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119771 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186335965 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119771 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186396038 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119771 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186487471 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186119771 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186487475 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186119771 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186571401 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119771 #edb/ref 1039 "Describing a Triangular Matrix" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119771 #edb/ref 1040 #edb/ref 17592186487484 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186119771 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186119585 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119771 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "1cca9b7c-358a-5f62-9a53-a696df0dd0ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119772 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119772 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120504 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119772 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262604 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119772 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262605 #ed