 "q-68754" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335970 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335970 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & -7 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 7 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is upper triangular\n- **II.** $A$ is lower triangular\n- **III.** $A+{A}^{T}$ is upper triangular" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186335970 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "deb97145-eaf3-5dcc-a36b-24fae2c52b5c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335970 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false, since $A$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & -7 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 7 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, since $A$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & -7 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 7 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true, since the result of $A+{A}^{T}$ has all the entries below the main diagonal equal to zero:\n\n$$\nA+{A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186342195 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186439283 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186342195 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186439284 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186342195 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186439285 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186342195 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74319" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342195 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342195 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix \n$D=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $D$ is upper triangular\n\n- **II.** $D$ is lower triangular\n\n- **III.** ${D}^{T}$ is upper triangular" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186342195 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "10915988-162b-5dec-9de2-5241d5fc3202" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342195 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false, since $D$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. All the entries above the main diagonal of $D$ are zeros:\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. All the entries below the main diagonal of ${D}^{T}$ are zeros:\n\n$$\n{D}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186396032 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396033 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396032 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396034 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396032 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396035 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396032 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396032 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396032 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396032 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396032 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186396035 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396032 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "bc095a3a-82a7-5c30-b624-4fd7e0ceae34" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396033 #edb/ref 1080 "Other" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396033 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396033 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "76cc8a4b-832c-56c2-8cf5-70501cfbad40" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396034 #edb/ref 1080 "Identity matrix" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396034 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396034 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9b6f508a-4794-5f61-a64e-b20147d225cf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396035 #edb/ref 1080 "Lower tri