ce they each have a non-zero element below the main diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{31} & =-1\\ne 0 \\\\ {c}_{32} & =2\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479928 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479918 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479928 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479922 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479928 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479933 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479928 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479928 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following matrices are upper triangular matrices?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 10 & -7 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479928 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "95bb49c4-214d-5ba6-82cc-f31f7a47c4fb" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479928 #edb/ref 1074 "The matrix $A$ is an upper triangular matrix since all the entries below the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nThe matrices $B$ and $C$ are *not* upper triangular matrices since they each have a non-zero element below the main diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{31} & =10\\ne 0 \\\\ {c}_{32} & =7\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443]}
